      "writtenOn": "2018-09-27T00:38:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes it\u0027s only applicable to default APN (i.e. internet). We only set it in two places.\n1. When the latest default APN data connection was successfully brought up using this data profile.\n2. When the user selects it in APN editor.\n\nThis is persistent across reboot.\n\nIf multiple profiles can serve default APN, only one profile will be marked as preferred.\n\nCan you explain why modem needs to know if the data profile is preferred? This flag only means we were able to use it for last data connection.\n\nFor the very first boot up, no data profile is preferred. Frameworks just try the first one from the database, and if it fails, it tries the second one.",
